:0,"created_at":"2025-07-02T04:16:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T15:58:31Z","closed_at":"2026-10-01T15:58:31Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot v4.4.1.stable\n- Reproducible in Godot v4.3.stable\n\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable (49a5bc7b6) - Fedora Linux 42 (Workstation Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Mesa Intel(R) UHD Graphics 620 (KBL GT2) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-8350U CPU @ 1.70GHz (8 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nResource file (.tres, res) owners is not visible in the owners list if set as custom GUI theme in project setting.\n\nThis could be a potentially fatal mistake during optimisation, as programmers and artists might delete the file, mistaking it for an orphaned file\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new theme file\n2. Apply the theme from Project Setting > General > GUI > Theme > Custom\n3. Go to FileSystem dock, then right click on the theme file. Select View Owners...\n4. You can see it has no owner despite its being used as a custom GUI theme project-wide.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.